# Native oracle: a clean tree must build its committed sources after an
# uncommitted edit was built and then reverted (SCV warm refresh,
# 2026-11-15: the reverted edit kept being compiled, `alpha 17` printed).
#
# Procedure (any admitted Stage 2 with SIMPLE_ABI_POLICY/_RECEIPT set):
#   1. cp -r this directory to scratch W; cd W; git init; git add src;
#      git commit -m base.
#   2. Build: <stage2> native-build --backend=cranelift --source src
#        --entry-closure src/main.spl --cache-dir C -o OUT   (prints alpha 13)
#   3. sed -i 's/x \* 3 + 1/x * 3 + 5/' src/alpha.spl; build again into a
#      fresh OUT (prints alpha 17).
#   4. git checkout src/alpha.spl (also: git stash, or write the old bytes
#      back by hand); build again into a fresh OUT and a FRESH cache dir C2.
#      Must print alpha 13. Before the fix it printed alpha 17: the SCV
#      inventory under W/build/scv kept the edited row.
#
# The fix records the dirty tracked paths of each published generation in a
# sidecar (build/scv/compile-events/dirty/<inventory digest>.paths) that older
# binaries never read; they keep working unchanged (with the old bug). When
# CURRENT names a generation with no sidecar (pre-fix store, or one an older
# binary published), the next refresh re-lists and re-hashes the whole tree
# once: 54.7 s wall, 1.0 GB max RSS for 46,322 sources on this repo
# (seed-interpreted, aarch64, 2026-11-15). Native Stage 2 on the same tree: about
# 30 s added to one build (74.7 s with the re-list against ~44 s warm).
# Known limit: paths marked assume-unchanged or skip-worktree are invisible
# to `git status`, so a revert under either flag is still not detected.
# Expected stdout:
# alpha 13
use alpha.{alpha_value}

fn main() -> i64:
    print("alpha {alpha_value(4)}")
    0
